    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1151">

                <pb facs="1409" n="1395" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.33112 RP/8–1045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-10T17:00:00-03:00">August 10, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>520. Bill on elimination Axis firms (despatch 6151, August 1<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d1151-f1"/>) was presented to Congress last night without change.
                    Intervention is being enforced effectively and will probably lead to liquidation
                    of many firms before enactment bill.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
